"09_filer.mst — the loose methods that start a view-resource read.

 `Array>>stbInFiler` is filed onto `Core.Array` by `Dolphin Literal Filer.pax`
 rather than declared in a `.cls`, so the class translator never sees it. It
 is one line, and it is the doorway to the whole mechanism:

     View>>loadViewResource: aResourceArray withContext: c forEdit: e
         filer := aResourceArray stbInFiler.
         child := filer isUpgrading: e; context: c; basicNext.
         [filer evaluateDeferredActions] ifCurtailed: [child destroy].
         ^child

 Loaded from `st/mvp_compat` because `STLInFiler` is translated into `st/mvp`,
 which loads after `st/dolphin_compat` — the reopen has to come after the
 class it names exists."

Array extend [
    "Dolphin's own body, verbatim. The resource is a literal array; the STL
     filer reads it as a stream of tokens."
    stbInFiler [ ^STLInFiler on: self readStream ]
]
